n \u03b8 \u221a3)/2, cos \u03b8 )\n\nSo, coordinates in Cartesian:\n\nA: (0, 0, 1)\n\nB: (sin \u03b8, 0, cos \u03b8)\n\nC: (- sin \u03b8 / 2, (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2, cos \u03b8)\n\nD: (- sin \u03b8 / 2, - (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2, cos \u03b8)\n\nNow, let's compute the volume of tetrahedron ABCD. The formula using coordinates is:\n\nVolume = | det([AB, AC, AD]) | / 6\n\nBut maybe it's easier to compute vectors from A to B, A to C, A to D, then compute the scalar triple product.\n\nWait, vectors AB, AC, AD:\n\nVector AB = B - A = (sin \u03b8, 0, cos \u03b8 - 1)\n\nVector AC = C - A = (- sin \u03b8 / 2, (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2, cos \u03b8 - 1)\n\nVector AD = D - A = (- sin \u03b8 / 2, - (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2, cos \u03b8 - 1)\n\nSo, the scalar triple product AB \u00b7 (AC \u00d7 AD) is the determinant of the matrix formed by these three vectors.\n\nLet me compute that determinant.\n\nFirst, let's write the vectors as columns:\n\nAB = [ sin \u03b8, 0, cos \u03b8 - 1 ]\n\nAC = [ -sin \u03b8 / 2, (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2, cos \u03b8 - 1 ]\n\nAD = [ -sin \u03b8 / 2, - (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2, cos \u03b8 - 1 ]\n\nSo, the determinant is:\n\n| sin \u03b8         -sin \u03b8 / 2        -sin \u03b8 / 2      |\n\n| 0             (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2     - (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2  |\n\n| cos \u03b8 - 1     cos \u03b8 - 1         cos \u03b8 - 1       |\n\nCalculating the determinant:\n\nFirst, expand along the first row.\n\nsin \u03b8 * det [ (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2, - (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2 ]\n\n           [ cos \u03b8 - 1,     cos \u03b8 - 1 ]\n\nMinus (-sin \u03b8 / 2) * det [ 0, - (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2 ]\n\n                         [ cos \u03b8 - 1, cos \u03b8 - 1 ]\n\nPlus (-sin \u03b8 / 2) * det [ 0, (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2 ]\n\n                        [ cos \u03b8 - 1, cos \u03b8 - 1 ]\n\nLet's compute each minor:\n\nFirst minor (for sin \u03b8 term):\n\ndet [ (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2, - (sin \u03b8 \u221a3)/2 ]\n\n    [ cos \u03b8 - 1,     cos \u03b8 - 1 ]\n\n= ( (sin \u03b8 \u221