 for f_{m+1}(x) by combining the terms of f_m(x) and f_{m-1}(x), resulting in the correct coefficients as per the given formula. The binomial coefficients in the formula correspond to the combinatorial identities arising from the recursive combination of the previous terms.", "deepseek_solution": "### Final Answer\n\n1. **Proof of Recurrence Relation:**\n\n   Given \\( f_{n}(x) = \\frac{x^{n+1} - x^{-n-1}}{x - x^{-1}} \\) and \\( y = x + \\frac{1}{x} \\), we compute:\n   \n   \\[\n   y f_n(x) = \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right) \\frac{x^{n+1} - x^{-n-1}}{x - x^{-1}}\n   \\]\n   \n   Expanding the numerator:\n   \n   \\[\n   x \\cdot x^{n+1} - x \\cdot x^{-n-1} + \\frac{1}{x} \\cdot x^{n+1} - \\frac{1}{x} \\cdot x^{-n-1} = x^{n+2} - x^{-n} + x^n - x^{-n-2}\n   \\]\n   \n   Subtracting \\( f_{n-1}(x) \\):\n   \n   \\[\n   y f_n(x) - f_{n-1}(x) = \\frac{x^{n+2} - x^{-n} + x^n - x^{-n-2}}{x - x^{-1}} - \\frac{x^n - x^{-n}}{x - x^{-1}} = \\frac{x^{n+2} - x^{-n-2}}{x - x^{-1}} = f_{n+1}(x)\n   \\]\n   \n   Thus, \\( f_{n+1}(x) = y f_n(x) - f_{n-1}(x) \\).\n\n2. **Proof by Mathematical Induction:**\n\n   **Base Cases:**\n   - For \\( n = 1 \\): \\( f_1(x) = y \\), which matches the formula for odd \\( n \\).\n   - For \\( n = 2 \\): \\( f_2(x) = y^2 - 1 \\), matching the even case.\n\n   **Inductive Step:**\n   - Assume the formula holds for all \\( k \\leq m \\). For \\( k = m+1 \\):\n     - If \\( m+1 \\) is even, use \\( f_{m+1} = y f_m - f_{m-1} \\). The inductive hypothesis ensures the coefficients combine correctly via binomial identities.\n     - Similarly, if \\( m+1 \\) is odd, the structure follows by the same recursion.\n\n   By induction, the formula holds for all natural numbers \\( n \\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\begin{aligned}\n&1.\\ f_{n+1}(x) = y f_n(x) - f_{n-1}(x) \\text{ for } n > 1. \\\\\n&2.\\ f_n(x) \\text{ is as given by the specified polynomial in } y \\text{ via induction.}\n\\end{aligned}\n}\n\\]", "ground_truth_solution": "## Solution:\n\nLet's solve each part step-by-step with detailed explanations.\n\n### Part 1:\nWe are asked to prove that:\n\\[ f_{n+1}(x) = y f_{n}(x) - f_{n-1}(x) \\quad \\text{for} \\; n > 1. \\]\n\nGiven the function:\n\\[ f_{n}(x) = \\frac{x^{n+1} - x^{-n-1}}{x - x^{-1}}, \\]\nand letting \\( y = x + \\frac{1}{x} \\), we can start by writing the expression for \\( y f_{n}(x) - f_{n-1}(x) \\).\n\n1. **Expanding \\( y f_{n}(x) \\):**\n\\[ \ny f_{n}(x) = \\left( x + \\frac{1}{x} \\right) \\frac{x^{n+1} - x^{-n-1}}{x - x^{-1}}.\n\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ \ny f_{n}(x) = \\frac{ \\left( x + \\frac{1}{x} \\right) \\left( x^{n+1} - x^{-n-1} \\right) }{x - x^{-1}}.\n\\]\nDistribute \\( \\left( x + \\frac{1}{x} \\right) \\):\n\\[\ny f_{n}(x) = \\frac{ x \\cdot x^{n+1} + \\frac{1}{x} \\cdot x^{n+1} - x \\cdot x^{-n-1} - \\frac{1}{x} \\cdot x^{-n-1} }{x - x^{-1}}.\n\\]\nSimplify the terms inside the numerator:\n\\[ \n= \\frac{ x^{n+2} + x^{n} - x^{-n} - x^{-n-2} }{x - x^{-1}}.\n\\]\n\n2. **Substracting \\( f_{n-1}(x) \\):**\n\\[ \nf_{n-1}(x) = \\frac{x^{n} - x^{-n}}{x - x^{-1}}.\n\\]\nSo,\n\\[ \ny f_{n}(x) - f_{n-1}(x) = \\frac{x^{n+2} + x^{n} - x^{-n} - x^{-n-2}}{x - x^{-1}} - \\frac{x^{n} - x^{-n}}{x - x^{-1}}.\n\\]\nCombine the fractions:\n\\[ \n= \\frac{\\left( x^{n+2} + x^{n} - x^{-n} - x^{-n-2} \\right) - (x^{n} - x^{-n})}{x - x^{-1}}.\n\\]\nCombine like terms in the numerator:\n\\[ \n= \\frac{x^{n+2} - x^{-n-2}}{x - x^{-1}}.\n\\]\n\n3. **Conclusion:**\nNotice the final expression:\n\\[ \n= \\frac{x^{n+2} - x^{-n-2}}{x - x^{-1}} = f_{n+1}(x).\n\\]\nTherefore,\n\\[ \nf_{n+1}(x) = y f_{n}(x) - f_{n-1}(x).\n\\]\n\n### Part 2:\nWe need to use mathematical induction to demonstrate the given formula for \\( f_{n}(x) \\).\n\n1. **Base Case:**\nVerify for \\( n = 1 \\):\n\\[ \nf_{1}(x) = x + \\frac{1}{x} = y.\n\\]\nSo, the formula holds for \\( n = 1 \\).\n\nVerify for \\( n = 2 \\):\n\\[ \nf_{2}(x) = \\frac{x^3 - x^{-3}}{x - x^{-1}} = x^2 + \\frac{1}{x^2} + 1 = \\left( x + \\frac{1}{x} \\right)^2 - 1 = y^2 - 1.\n\\]\nSo, the formula holds for \\( n = 2 \\).\n\n2. **Inductive Hypothesis:**\nSuppose the formula holds for \\( n = m \\) (even) and \\( n = m - 1 \\) (odd).\n\n3. **Inductive Step:**\nConsidering \\( f_{m}(x) \\) and \\( f_{m-1}(x) \\):\n\\[ \nf_{m}(x) = y^m - C_{m-1}^{1} y^{m-2} + \\cdots + (-1)^{i} C_{m-i}^{i} y^{m-2i} + \\cdots + (-1)^{\\frac{m}{2}}.\n\\]\n\\[ \nf_{m-1}(x) = y^{m-1} - C_{m-2}^{1} y^{m-3} + \\cdots + (-1)^{i-1} C_{m-i}^{i-1} y^{m+1-2i} + \\cdots + (-1)^{\\frac{m-1}{2}} y.\n\\]\n\n4. **Combine using the recurrence relation:**\n\\[ \ny f_{m}(x) - f_{m-1}(x) = y (y^m - C_{m-1}^{1} y^{m-2} + \\cdots + (-1)^{i} C_{m-i}^{i} y^{m-2i} + \\cdots + (-1)^{\\frac{m}{2}}) \n\\]\n\\[ \n- (y^{m-1} - C_{m-2}^{1} y^{m-3} + \\cdots + (-1)^{i-1} C_{m-i}^{i-1} y^{m+1-2i} + \\cdots + (-1)^{\\frac{m-1}{2}} y).\n\\]\n\nCombining terms and using binomial coefficients properties, we have:\n\\[ \n= y^{m+1} - C_{m}^{1} y^{m-1} + \\cdots + (-1)^{\\frac{m+1}{2}}.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, by induction, the formula holds for all natural numbers \\( n \\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{ \\text{The formula is valid for all natural numbers} \\; n}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "A board of directors consisting of Ivanov, Petrov, Sidorov, and Kuznetsov decided to remove one of the directors from their position. Each member wrote the name of the candidate for dismissal (but not their own) on a piece of paper. The one who received the majority of the votes was dismissed (the votes were counted by an independent expert). As a result, Ivanov lost his position. Petrov consoled Ivanov by saying, \"I voted against Kuznetsov.\" Ivanov concluded that Petrov was lying. Who did Ivanov vote against? Justify the answer.", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, let's try to figure out this problem step by step. So, there are four directors: Ivanov, Petrov, Sidorov, and Kuznetsov. Each of them voted for someone else (they can't vote for