ed and 2 white balls\n\n5. **Calculate the total number of white balls:**\n   - White balls in boxes with 1 white ball each:\n     \\[\n     27 \\text{ boxes} \\times 1 \\text{ white ball} = 27 \\text{ white balls}\n     \\]\n   - White balls in boxes with 2 white balls each (and 1 red):\n     \\[\n     43 \\text{ boxes} \\times 2 \\text{ white balls} = 86 \\text{ white balls}\n     \\]\n   - White balls in boxes with 3 white balls each:\n     \\[\n     15 \\text{ boxes} \\times 3 \\text{ white balls} = 45 \\text{ white balls}\n     \\]\n\n   Adding all the white balls together:\n   \\[\n   27 + 86 + 45 = 158\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion\nThus, the total number of white balls is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{158}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "In a certain country, the airline system is arranged so that each city is connected by airlines with no more than three other cities, and from each city, you can reach any other city with at most one transfer. What is the maximum number of cities that can be in this country?", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, so I need to figure out the maximum number of cities in this airline system where each city is connected to no more than three others, and you can get from any city to any other with at most one transfer. Let me start by breaking down the problem.\n\nFirst, let's rephrase the problem in graph theory terms. Each city is a node, and each airline route is an edge. The condition that each city is connected to no more than three others means the graph has a maximum degree of 3. The other condition is that any two nodes are connected by a path of length at most 2. So the diameter of the graph is at most 2. We need to find the maximum number of nodes such a graph can have with these constraints.\n\nI remember that in graph theory, there's a concept called a \"Moore graph\" which is a regular graph where the diameter is minimized for the given degree. For diameter 2, the Moore 